title: Don't issue a number twice when new runs under two parents at once
created: 2026-10-24T09:49:14Z
updated: 2026-10-24T09:49:19Z
effort: S
area: cli
handoff:

Ported from IDOL's vendored copy (IDOL 1363), where it was found and fixed.

new scans for the highest number before it takes the tracker lock, and
inside the lock tries mkdir on successive numbers. mkdir only sees
siblings, so a number another new issued under a different parent since
the scan was taken again: a top-level ticket and a child created at once
both came out as the same number, and every needs: on it became
ambiguous.

Fix: inside the lock, skip any number already in .pidly/.n/. Every new
registers its number before unlocking, so the registry holds it even
when the directory sits under another parent.

Done when tests/new.sh pins both a new that queued on the lock while a
child took the next number, and a race of top-level and child creations.
